From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:34:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: mtu3: let a suspended bus suspend the system

ssusb_gadget_suspend() refuses a system suspend whenever the gadget is
connected. Connected is cleared only by a disconnect, which the MAC sees
through VBUS. The Gemini's PHY forces the B-session valid, so a removed
cable is never seen as a disconnect: the controller only sees the bus go
idle and reports a bus suspend, and the system can then never suspend on
battery (-EBUSY from mtu3 in the station's first s2idle test).

A suspended bus means the host is not using the link: it is asleep or
gone. Track the bus suspend (set on the suspend interrupt, cleared on
resume and reset) and let the system suspend while it lasts; an active
link still refuses, as before.
---
 drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3.h        | 1 +
 drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c   | 7 ++++++-
 drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_gadget.c | 3 +++
 3 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3.h b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3.h
index ba5a63669..320a5e37e 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3.h
@@ -367,6 +367,7 @@ struct mtu3 {
 	unsigned delayed_status:1;
 	unsigned gen2cp:1;
 	unsigned connected:1;
+	unsigned bus_suspended:1;
 	unsigned async_callbacks:1;
 	unsigned separate_fifo:1;
 
diff --git a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c
index 66dbfe170..ecae7a057 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_core.c
@@ -1037,7 +1037,12 @@ int ssusb_gadget_suspend(struct ssusb_mtk *ssusb, pm_message_t msg)
 	if (!mtu->gadget_driver)
 		return 0;
 
-	if (mtu->connected)
+	/*
+	 * A suspended bus is either a sleeping host or, where the PHY forces
+	 * the session valid and no VBUS drop is seen, a removed cable: neither
+	 * is using the link, so the system may suspend too.
+	 */
+	if (mtu->connected && !mtu->bus_suspended)
 		return -EBUSY;
 
 	mtu3_dev_suspend(mtu);
diff --git a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_gadget.c b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_gadget.c
index da29f4679..aa800db6b 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_gadget.c
@@ -728,6 +728,7 @@ void mtu3_gadget_cleanup(struct mtu3 *mtu)
 void mtu3_gadget_resume(struct mtu3 *mtu)
 {
 	dev_dbg(mtu->dev, "gadget RESUME\n");
+	mtu->bus_suspended = 0;
 	if (mtu->async_callbacks && mtu->gadget_driver && mtu->gadget_driver->resume) {
 		spin_unlock(&mtu->lock);
 		mtu->gadget_driver->resume(&mtu->g);
@@ -739,6 +740,7 @@ void mtu3_gadget_resume(struct mtu3 *mtu)
 void mtu3_gadget_suspend(struct mtu3 *mtu)
 {
 	dev_dbg(mtu->dev, "gadget SUSPEND\n");
+	mtu->bus_suspended = 1;
 	if (mtu->async_callbacks && mtu->gadget_driver && mtu->gadget_driver->suspend) {
 		spin_unlock(&mtu->lock);
 		mtu->gadget_driver->suspend(&mtu->g);
@@ -763,6 +765,7 @@ void mtu3_gadget_disconnect(struct mtu3 *mtu)
 void mtu3_gadget_reset(struct mtu3 *mtu)
 {
 	dev_dbg(mtu->dev, "gadget RESET\n");
+	mtu->bus_suspended = 0;
 
 	/* report disconnect, if we didn't flush EP state */
 	if (mtu->g.speed != USB_SPEED_UNKNOWN)
-- 
2.43.0

